      "answer": "The customer whose issue started after the 2026-02-20 taxonomy rollout is BlueHarbor Logistics. The proposed proof plan to get them comfortable with renewal is a 7-10 business day proof involving updating index weighting and adding a mapping layer to translate new taxonomy terms to old query terms for the top 20 saved searches. The acceptance criteria include achieving a top-5 correct hit rate of at least 80%, no regression in suppression logic, and incident correlation latency under 200ms. This proof includes a 90-day professional services engagement at a fixed price of $48k, with a 30% discount if Orchestrator seats are expanded concurrently, and a conditional credit clause if the proof does not meet the agreed metrics within 10 business days [art_0bccc580184e, art_bd3560dfe194, art_c9970c1dc932].",
