      "answer": "The SCIM fields conflicting at Aureum were \"department\" and \"businessUnit.\" Merchant Services used businessUnit=merchant while Payments Ops used department=payments, causing ingestion normalization to fail collapsing these into a single canonical attribute, which led to the Rules Engine failing to match entity tags for routing approvals. Jin proposed a fast fix by adding a preprocessing rule in Signal Ingest to map businessUnit to department (or vice versa) and publish a normalized field for the correlator. This fix is a configuration-only change that can be hot-reloaded without requiring changes to Okta flows or appliance restarts, thus avoiding waiting on Okta change control. This approach allows immediate normalization and improved routing with low risk and no downtime during settlement windows. [art_79f625aafa16]",
